    "campaign": {
     "title": "Agency 4: How do you handle client licenses?",
     "email_subject": "How do you handle client licenses today?",
     "email_pre_header": "One question, and your answer goes straight to me.",
     "email_body": "<!-- wp:paragraph {\"fontSize\":\"filter-md\"} -->\n<p class=\"has-filter-md-font-size\">Hi {{contact.first_name|there}},</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>A couple of weeks ago your account was set up for an agency, but you haven't assigned a license to a client yet. That's fine. I'd like to learn why.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>How do you handle plugin licenses for your clients today? Do you buy them and keep them, have clients buy their own, or something else?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Please just reply. I read every answer, and it decides what we build next for agencies.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Zack Katz<br>Founder, GravityKit</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
